																		The Rube Effect
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-chombie-mazing" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7054200); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7054200&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606594343" alt="Dr Chombie Mazing" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7054200)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-chombie-mazing" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7054200); return false;" >Dr Chombie Mazing</a></span> <span class="odate time_1606415288 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2020 18:28</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4828761">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article, Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Drama/Emotional, Comedy, Joke</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Test and incident logs to be included. I intend to cross refence other works, but would like to ask permission from other authors before I commit to that. There will be accompanying Tales with the lore linked from the article.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Woman is infected with a &quot;virus&quot; of sorts that neutralizes nearby deadly threats with 'events' that work on a similar principle to the butterfly effect or a Rube Goldberg machine. It can manipulate any non-organic material to complete an event. The woman is incredulously unaware of her anomalous properties.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The virus is contagious but this is unknown by the majority of the Foundation at the time of the article's writing. Its effects are efficient but subtle. The Subject, as a teenager, is sent to live at the School for Children of Prominence. A short lived boarding school/orphanage program for children of Foundation personnel. The program caused a spike in unfit staff during a time period infamously known by experienced staff as LolFoundation. She is notably idiotic and it amazes her teachers that she actually graduates. Once she starts working for the Foundation as a junior researcher, her peers are dumbfounded that despite lacking all common sense she has yet to die. She unintentionally causes several small containment breaches, and one which most defiantly should have killed her. This prompts an investigation and her eventual classification as an SCP. After the article is submitted for review the higher ups begin to doubt the judgement of the lead researcher and try to have the SCP declassified due to 'lack of sufficient anomalous evidence'. 05's have started cracking down on unprofessional behavior causing the lead researcher to be shunned. The lead dives into a depressed drunken stupor. It remains to be seen if the Foundation will continue the lead's research and discover how to harness the power of this virus.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The virus isn't all powerful and it wont infect just anyone. It's host can still be injured and it will not prevent death due to biological means such as old age or venom. It is, however, very good at keeping its host alive. The Foundation would kill to have something like this for all of their field agents.</p>

