<p>Howdy hey! I'm <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5950867); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5950867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606588569" alt="KaraKatt" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5950867)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5950867); return false;">KaraKatt</a></span> and I'll be dropping a little bit of crit today!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Line&nbsp;by&nbsp;line&nbsp;and&nbsp;general&nbsp;thoughts.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;...</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<h2><span>Questions I Have While Reading Through</span></h2>
<blockquote>
<p>The virus is contagious but this is unknown by the Foundation at the time of the article's writing.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How do they find out that its a virus? They seem very blind to it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The Subject was the child of two researchers who were killed in a containment breach. She's sent to live at the School for Children of Prominence. A short lived boarding school/orphanage program for children of Foundation personnel. She is notably idiotic and it amazes her teachers that she actually graduates.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't entirely see how this is important to the over arching story. Like, it gives back story, but I don't think you're going to have a way to slide it into the actual SCP.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>After the article is submitted for review the higher ups begin to doubt the judgement of the lead researcher and try to have the SCP declassified due to 'lack or sufficient anomalous evidence'. The lead researcher is shunned and dives into a depressed drunken stupor.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would this lead to the Foundation shunning the researcher? If they just think its someone making things without evidence (or not enough) wouldn't they just shrug and give them a slap on the wrist?</p>
<hr />
<h2><span>Final notes</span></h2>
<p>Hmm, this is interesting, but I don't think its quite there yet. You have a cool idea and a sort of story, but it feels like its missing some key parts to actually get its idea across. If the Foundation doesn't try to do stuff with the virus, then how would the reader ever know its a virus or even useable to the Foundation? I would also like to put in here that, because you're writing a human, you're going to need to characterize her. That's not saying to shove in backstory, but it is to say that you're going to need to show her idiocy.</p>
<p>Good luck!</p>
</div>
